# Yuta

Local-first AI companion. Desktop shell is Tauri + Vite. Domain logic lives in `packages/*` so a future web app can reuse it.

- Keep packages focused. Do not import `@yuta/ai` from `@yuta/character-engine` or `@yuta/emotion-engine`.
- Character rendering consumes only `CharacterState`.
- AI output is JSON validated with Zod against the closed emotion/action lists in `@yuta/shared`.
- Orchestration stays in TypeScript. Rust is for FS, OS paths, lifecycle, and secret storage.
- Personal data stays on disk via the filesystem adapter. No cloud memory.
- User-supplied Gemini key only. Never ship or commit API keys. Never put production secrets in `.env`.
- Prefer extending an existing package over adding a new abstraction.
- No vector DB, cloud backend, or extra LLM providers unless explicitly requested.
- Comments only when needed. Prefix with `NOTE:`, `TODO:`, `FIXME:`, `HACK:`, or `BUG:`.
- No emojis in logs or comments.
- Reuse shared helpers. Do not duplicate retrieval, parsing, or UI primitives.
